WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:04.100
-Craven Trump supporters
like Senator Marco Rubio

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.767
are trying to downplay
the severity

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.367
of the federal
criminal investigation

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.200
into the classified materials

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.767
found at Trump's
Mar-a-Lago resort.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.100
Meanwhile,
a Trump-appointed judge

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.801
granted what legal scholars
across the political spectrum,

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.501
including Trump's own
former attorney general,

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:20.801
considered an absurd request
to slow down

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.534
the Justice Department's
investigations.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:23.868
So, you know...

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.267
that sucks.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.467
Oh, wait, I forgot.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.067
We do a whole segment
about stuff like that.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.234
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:32.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.968
♪♪

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:38.100
You know, we always joke
around the office here

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.767
about how the craziest
news stories

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.767
always seem to break
on Friday night

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.167
or when we have a week off

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.567
and how we wish we had a show
so we could talk about it.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.968
We've been off for four weeks,
and you know what happened

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:50.467
the Monday of our
first week off?

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.834
The FBI search of Mar-a-Lago.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.834
I was on vacation with my family
and I said to my wife,

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:59.167
"The feds found classified
documents at Trump's residence,

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.567
but we don't have shows
for a month.

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.968
What am I supposed to do now?"
And then she said to me,

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:06.467
"I don't know, maybe be a father
to your three children?"

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:08.667
And then I said a bunch
of stuff back to her,

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.434
but under my breath
while I was walking away

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:11.434
so she couldn't hear it.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:12.901
Point is...

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:15.601
...it's so nice to be back.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.601
And it wasn't just
Trump scandal stuff we missed.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:18.834
Joe Biden and the Democrats

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.834
strung together a bunch
of surprise victories

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.734
both legislatively
and politically,

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:24.100
bumping Biden's poll numbers

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.667
in hopes that Democrats
can hold onto power

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:28.100
as midterm season ramps up.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.434
And you can tell Biden's
got some pep in his step now.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.467
I mean, before
when he was slogging

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.234
through the doldrums
of his presidency

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.267
with record-low
approval ratings,

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:39.734
just getting COVID
over and over again

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.834
like they were accidentally
treating his COVID

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.734
with more COVID...

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:46.067
And he would do that thing
where he'd close his eyes

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:49.300
and lower his head whenever
a reporter asked him a question

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.100
like he was in physical pain.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.834
He looked like Chris Pine
at the Venice Film Festival.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:58.667
That was the posture of a man
who spent eight years

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:01.968
as vice president and thought,
"How hard could this job be?"

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:05.501
then got the job and immediately
realized it only looked easy

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.000
because Obama was
the one doing it.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.367
Obama made being president
look like a cross between

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:13.901
being a record producer
and an Instagram influencer.

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:17.200
"For more tutorials
on the debt ceiling, uhhh,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.534
smash that follow button."

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:21.033
But that was the old Biden.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.200
And look at him now.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.534
He's a completely
different guy,

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.434
as you can tell from
some of his recent rallies

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:28.000
where, among other things,
he championed a bill

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.801
to cap prescription drug prices
for Medicare patients

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.667
and touted the power
of women voters.

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:36.367
-We beat pharma this year.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:39.701
We beat pharma this year,
and it mattered.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.934
We're gonna change
people's lives.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:45.200
MAGA Republicans don't have
a clue about the power of women.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.534
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.501
Let me tell you something.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.167
They are about to find out.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:53.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:55.300
Oh. Oh, yeah.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.300
Oh, yeah.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.634
-He's got...

00:02:58.634 --> 00:02:59.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.834
Got so much confidence now.

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:05.501
He's turned into Barry White.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.667
It's too bad those guys
never got to work together.

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.100
-♪ Can't get enough
of your love, babe ♪

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.067
-Oh. Oh, yeah.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:16.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.267
-Anyway, Biden is clearly
laser-focused

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:23.767
on the growing list
of accomplishments

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.067
during his tenure

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.234
and a string of big victories
in special elections

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:29.868
that have revived Democrats'
political fortunes.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:32.934
But he has one
very formidable obstacle

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:34.300
in his way -- Donald Trump,

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.934
a rival with unparalleled
political instincts.

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:39.234
A man with his finger
on the pulse of the electorate.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.400
A candidate with the foresight
and discipline

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.367
to stay strictly on message

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.634
and make sure he's connecting
with voters

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:48.567
over the kitchen-table issues
they care about, like this.

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.901
-If you want to see

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.567
a dead bird cemetery,

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.033
go under a windmill sometime.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.734
It's not a pretty sight.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:56.901
-Okay, but...

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:59.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:03.767
What if I don't want to see
a dead bird cemetery?

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.567
Is that an option?

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:09.067
Also, what do you mean,
"dead bird cemetery"?

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:16.200
Is there such a thing
as an alive bird cemetery?

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.868
[As Trump]
I bury them up to their necks.

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.868
They never stop chirping.

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:21.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:23.767
[Normal voice] Trump's windmill
obsession has been going on

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:24.868
for like a decade now,

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.367
and it's somehow
getting creepier.

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:28.634
He used to complain about them
being ugly and noisy,

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.100
and now he's basically the kid
from "Stand By Me."

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.701
"You guys want to see
a dead bird cemetery?"

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:34.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:36.934
I'd hate to get sight-seeing
advice from Trump.

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.033
What should we do
while we're in New York, Donald?

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:42.667
[As Trump] There's a lot of dead
geese by the airport.

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:44.000
You should check that out.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.367
Remember,
Sully Sullenberger, he saved --

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:50.200
he saved that airplane,
but he killed a lot of geese.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:54.033
Nobody remembers the dead geese.
But I do. I do.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:55.834
I remember once
a goose came up to me --

00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:57.934
big goose, strong goose --

00:04:57.934 --> 00:05:00.567
tears in his eyes
and running down his bill --

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:03.567
Beak? I don't know.

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:04.634
And he said to me --

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:06.100
I'll never forget
what he said to me.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.100
He said, "Sir...

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.267
Honk!"

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:09.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:11.467
[Normal voice] But I guess...

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:15.934
I guess if I was Donald Trump
and I was also under

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:18.067
like 97 different
criminal investigations,

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:20.501
I, too, would be trying
to draw America's focus

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:22.834
to the nation's
dead bird cemeteries.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:24.734
I mean, the CFO
of his family company

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:27.300
just pleaded guilty to tax fraud
and promised to cooperate

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.067
in the investigation
of the Trump Organization.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.667
The state attorney general
is investigating

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:31.934
his company for fraud.

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:33.334
The Fulton County
district attorney

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:35.534
is investigating Trump's
threatening phone call

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:36.934
to the Georgia
secretary of state

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:38.968
to try to overturn
the state's election results.

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:41.901
There are at least two federal
grand juries that we know of,

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:45.200
investigating the January 6th
insurrection and a scheme

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.701
to submit counterfeit electors
to keep Trump in power.

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:49.868
And of course, now perhaps
the most serious them all,

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:51.400
a criminal investigation
into Trump

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.434
apparently just jacking a bunch

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.767
of closely guarded government
secrets from the White House

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:59.667
and keeping them in the closet
of his gold-plated swamp hotel

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:02.501
the way the rest of us hoard
old receipts from CVS.

00:06:02.501 --> 00:06:04.567
And just as a quick refresher,

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.501
since the month of August
has been, in news terms,

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:09.200
about three centuries long,
the materials the FBI seized

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.434
weren't just innocuous
government documents.

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.300
They were reportedly
some of the most sensitive

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.000
documents the government has.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.133
-The FBI found 184 classified
documents in 15 boxes.

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:24.300
That includes 25 documents
marked as top secret.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.300
-According to the FBI,
some of the material was marked

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.734
with the highest levels
of classification that exists,

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:32.634
material that is meant
to be held

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:35.801
only in secure
government facilities,

00:06:35.801 --> 00:06:39.133
not at a private club
where basically anyone can pay

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:41.267
for a membership
and wander around.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.467
Arguably, the agents
most alarming finding

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:46.067
that we were able to see
in this redacted version

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:48.701
was that the boxes contained
classified information

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:51.567
that came from
human intelligence sources,

00:06:51.567 --> 00:06:54.434
meaning that if the documents
were mishandled or leaked

00:06:54.434 --> 00:06:55.834
or transmitted,

00:06:55.834 --> 00:07:00.601
it could compromise the identity
of American intelligence assets.

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:03.801
-The government says it found
more than 40 folders

00:07:03.801 --> 00:07:06.567
with "classified" markings
that were empty.

00:07:06.567 --> 00:07:09.367
-So, Donald Trump gets to steal
highly classified material

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:11.000
containing some of the
government's most closely

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.501
guarded secrets
from the White House,

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:15.734
but if I do so much as borrow
a stamp from the supply closet,

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:18.567
I get a bill for 60 cents
from an all-caps email from H.R.

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:20.767
that says, "Reminder: Office
supplies are exclusive property

00:07:20.767 --> 00:07:22.167
of NBC Universal

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:24.567
and cannot be used
for personal business."

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:25.834
So, let me see
if I'm following this.

00:07:25.834 --> 00:07:27.868
The FBI found
national defense documents

00:07:27.868 --> 00:07:29.968
that could potentially
compromise the identities

00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:32.033
of American personnel --
documents with some

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:34.267
of the highest classification
markings that exist,

00:07:34.267 --> 00:07:36.567
in the storage closet
of Donald Trump's

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:38.968
highly secured
fortified compound --

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:40.167
Oh, I'm sorry.
I read that wrong.

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:42.167
In the basement
of Donald Trump's Palm Beach

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:45.834
wedding venue for dentists
and their second wives,

00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:47.968
where a bunch of spies
or tourists

00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:49.400
or Trump's lumpy adult sons

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.400
could just wander around
and see them.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.901
And on top of that, some of the
classified folders were empty.

00:07:53.901 --> 00:07:56.834
Where did the documents
that were in those folders go?

00:07:56.834 --> 00:07:59.200
Has Trump been giving them out
as party gifts to club members?

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.634
When you sit down at your table,

00:08:00.634 --> 00:08:02.334
does the menu give you
a choice of chicken,

00:08:02.334 --> 00:08:04.667
fish, or nuclear codes?

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:06.667
All this time,
I thought foreign spies

00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:08.000
had to go to extreme lengths

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.000
to infiltrate highly secure
government buildings.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.167
And in reality,
it turns out all they need to do

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:13.968
is sidle up to Trump
at the omelet bar.

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:15.667
[Russian accent]
Hello. My name is John Smith.

00:08:15.667 --> 00:08:17.334
I would like Denver omelet.

00:08:17.334 --> 00:08:18.667
[As Trump]
The Denver omelet is great,

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:21.000
but wouldn't you rather have
some troop locations?

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.100
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:24.100
[Normal voice]
Now, as a delay tactic,

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.367
Trump asked a judge to appoint
what's known as a special master

00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:28.767
to sift through the documents

00:08:28.767 --> 00:08:31.167
and separate out anything
that's privileged or personal.

00:08:31.167 --> 00:08:34.501
And yesterday, a judge appointed
by Trump and handpicked

00:08:34.501 --> 00:08:36.167
by the right-wing
Federalist Society

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:37.634
granted that request,

00:08:37.634 --> 00:08:39.334
despite the fact
that legal experts

00:08:39.334 --> 00:08:42.200
across the political spectrum
consider the request absurd.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.734
Various legal experts
told The New York Times

00:08:44.734 --> 00:08:48.000
yesterday that the decision
was "genuinely unprecedented,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.033
deeply problematic,
and thin at best,"

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:53.000
with one even going so far
as to claim that "to any lawyer

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.534
with serious federal criminal
court experience

00:08:55.534 --> 00:08:58.567
who is being honest,
this ruling is laughingly bad."

00:08:58.567 --> 00:09:00.634
Well, sure, if you're gonna
limit it to lawyers with serious

00:09:00.634 --> 00:09:02.567
federal criminal court
experience, we're being honest.

00:09:02.567 --> 00:09:04.934
What about the lawyers
that don't fit that category?

00:09:04.934 --> 00:09:07.968
Did the biased New York Times
interview any of them?

00:09:07.968 --> 00:09:11.601
[As Giuliani] If you ask me,
this ruling makes perfect sense.

00:09:11.601 --> 00:09:13.601
Almost as much sense
as marrying my cousin.

00:09:13.601 --> 00:09:15.367
It's a wedding
and a family reunion.

00:09:15.367 --> 00:09:16.968
Two birds with one windmill.

00:09:16.968 --> 00:09:19.634
[Normal voice]
Even Trump's own

00:09:19.634 --> 00:09:22.067
former attorney general,
Bill Barr, who you may recall

00:09:22.067 --> 00:09:23.300
did everything in his power

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:24.901
to shield Trump from
the Mueller investigation,

00:09:24.901 --> 00:09:27.234
thought the special master
request was nonsense.

00:09:27.234 --> 00:09:30.334
-Well, I think the whole idea
of a special master

00:09:30.334 --> 00:09:32.400
is a bit of a red herring.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.000
The only documents
that have been taken,

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:39.100
it seems to me, that there's
a legitimate concern

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.300
about keeping away
from the government

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:44.400
and insulating the government
from would be documents

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:47.501
relating to his private
lawyer communications --

00:09:47.501 --> 00:09:51.167
him as an individual
and his outside lawyers.

00:09:51.167 --> 00:09:52.934
If there's stuff
like that, fine.

00:09:52.934 --> 00:09:54.100
Identify it.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.100
There doesn't appear
to be much of it.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.734
I'm not sure you need
a special master to identify it.

00:09:58.734 --> 00:10:01.267
Any other documents that were
seized, like news clippings

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:03.467
and other things that were
in the boxes containing

00:10:03.467 --> 00:10:07.634
the classified information,
those were seizable

00:10:07.634 --> 00:10:10.334
under the warrant
because they show the conditions

00:10:10.334 --> 00:10:13.901
under which the classified
information was being held.

00:10:13.901 --> 00:10:15.367
So, I think it's a red herring.

00:10:15.367 --> 00:10:17.968
-Even Bill Barr is calling this
special master thing bull[bleep]

00:10:17.968 --> 00:10:19.701
and he's the guy
who preemptively released

00:10:19.701 --> 00:10:21.434
misleading snippets
of the Mueller report

00:10:21.434 --> 00:10:23.734
to make it look like
the report exonerated Trump

00:10:23.734 --> 00:10:25.667
when the reality
was the exact opposite.

00:10:25.667 --> 00:10:27.534
And that's when you know
things are bad --

00:10:27.534 --> 00:10:29.367
when your own henchmen
turn on you.

00:10:29.367 --> 00:10:30.767
It would be like if Wally

00:10:30.767 --> 00:10:32.834
started doing cue cards
for James Corden.

00:10:32.834 --> 00:10:34.501
-Sorry, Seth.
He let me have my own segment

00:10:34.501 --> 00:10:37.734
called "Card-Pool Wally-oke."

00:10:37.734 --> 00:10:38.868
-Wally!

00:10:38.868 --> 00:10:40.033
What was Paul like?

00:10:40.033 --> 00:10:41.834
-Oh, Paul was super nice.
Very down to earth.

00:10:41.834 --> 00:10:42.901
You'd like him.

00:10:42.901 --> 00:10:44.167
Ehh, I'm not sure
he'd like you, but --

00:10:44.167 --> 00:10:45.334
-Wally!

00:10:45.334 --> 00:10:47.000
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.601 --> 00:10:50.234
But, you know, all else aside,
I have to say,

00:10:50.234 --> 00:10:51.968
I'm actually quite impressed
by the courage

00:10:51.968 --> 00:10:54.667
and bravery many Republicans
have shown in criticizing Trump

00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:57.067
for this obviously
brazen criminal act.

00:10:57.067 --> 00:10:58.567
They're finally showing
some spine.

00:10:58.567 --> 00:11:01.467
Like Marco Rubio,
who had some pretty harsh words

00:11:01.467 --> 00:11:03.701
for Trump's mishandling
of classified information.

00:11:03.701 --> 00:11:05.367
-Even if it wasn't
marked classified,

00:11:05.367 --> 00:11:06.634
I would know it's classified

00:11:06.634 --> 00:11:08.200
because there are
other indicators

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.033
in those documents
that make it clear.

00:11:10.033 --> 00:11:11.901
In fact, just by reading
the kind of information,

00:11:11.901 --> 00:11:13.968
you know that it has to be
classified.

00:11:13.968 --> 00:11:15.367
Sometimes it's not
just classified

00:11:15.367 --> 00:11:16.934
because of the information,

00:11:16.934 --> 00:11:18.934
but because embedded
in the information

00:11:18.934 --> 00:11:20.100
is how it was acquired.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.634
You don't want your adversaries

00:11:21.634 --> 00:11:23.133
to know
how you acquire information.

00:11:23.133 --> 00:11:25.334
-And the risk of that is...?
-The risk of that

00:11:25.334 --> 00:11:27.834
is that we're giving opponents
of this government

00:11:27.834 --> 00:11:30.234
or adversaries some insight
into our thinking,

00:11:30.234 --> 00:11:31.501
into our decision-making,

00:11:31.501 --> 00:11:33.234
and it provides them
most certainly an advantage

00:11:33.234 --> 00:11:34.901
in the national security realm.

00:11:34.901 --> 00:11:37.200
-Thank you, Senator Rubio.
A true profile in courage.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:38.367
Say what you want about the man,

00:11:38.367 --> 00:11:39.767
but at least
he's finally speaking up

00:11:39.767 --> 00:11:41.934
and taking on Donald Trump's
obvious criminality

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:44.100
and abuses of power
and warning Americans

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:46.200
of the risk Trump posed to --
Wuzzat?

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.367
Oh, all those clips
were from 2015

00:11:48.367 --> 00:11:51.000
and he was talking about
Hillary Clinton's emails?

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.634
[ Laughter ]
Oh, man.

00:11:52.634 --> 00:11:55.801
What a silly
and unexpected mix-up.

00:11:55.801 --> 00:11:59.000
This is what happens
when you take a month off.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.067
You mess up and you play
a clip package

00:12:01.067 --> 00:12:03.267
that inadvertently proves
how craven and hypocritical

00:12:03.267 --> 00:12:06.200
Trump supporters are,
which was not my goal.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:07.701
[ Laughter ]

00:12:07.701 --> 00:12:09.901
I apologize to you, Senator.

00:12:09.901 --> 00:12:12.567
[ Laughter ]

00:12:12.567 --> 00:12:14.067
Let's hear what
Rubio actually had to say

00:12:14.067 --> 00:12:15.567
about Trump's stolen
classified materials.

00:12:15.567 --> 00:12:16.934
I'm sure he was consistent.

00:12:16.934 --> 00:12:18.267
-This is really, at its core,

00:12:18.267 --> 00:12:20.167
a storage argument
that they're making, right?

00:12:20.167 --> 00:12:22.434
They're arguing there
are documents there.

00:12:22.434 --> 00:12:24.534
They don't deny that he should
have access to those documents.

00:12:24.534 --> 00:12:27.000
What they deny is that
they were not properly stored.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:30.334
I don't think a fight
over storage of documents

00:12:30.334 --> 00:12:32.334
is worthy of what they've done.

00:12:32.334 --> 00:12:35.267
-I'm sorry, you think
this is a storage issue?

00:12:35.267 --> 00:12:37.501
The Justice Department
shouldn't have sent the FBI,

00:12:37.501 --> 00:12:39.434
but rather Marie Kondo?

00:12:39.434 --> 00:12:40.767
[ Laughter ]

00:12:40.767 --> 00:12:42.801
[As Trump] I need your help
sparking joy, Marie.

00:12:42.801 --> 00:12:45.634
I've got papers everywhere.
My mood is foul.

00:12:45.634 --> 00:12:47.334
Plus, someone keeps
knocking over

00:12:47.334 --> 00:12:49.400
the tombstones
in my dead bird cemetery.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.767
Would -- Would you like to see
my dead bird cemetery?

00:12:51.767 --> 00:12:53.033
What's that, Marie?

00:12:53.033 --> 00:12:54.934
You don't need to say "dead"
when you say "cemetery"?

00:12:54.934 --> 00:12:57.100
Why is that, Marie? Why?

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:59.200
Oh, because cemetery
implies the birds are dead.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:03.501
Look at that -- you're already
tidying up my grammar, Marie.

00:13:03.501 --> 00:13:06.234
I think we're gonna
get along just fine.

00:13:06.234 --> 00:13:08.734
[Normal voice] When it comes
down to it, it's very simple.

00:13:08.734 --> 00:13:10.767
It's a question of whether
or not everyone,

00:13:10.767 --> 00:13:12.601
including Donald Trump,
is equal under the law.

00:13:12.601 --> 00:13:14.634
Because if anyone else
was caught with those

00:13:14.634 --> 00:13:15.968
documents in their possession,

00:13:15.968 --> 00:13:17.467
they'd face consequences
immediately.

00:13:17.467 --> 00:13:20.133
Mar-a-Lago is no place
for top secret documents.

00:13:20.133 --> 00:13:21.834
The only place less secure
would be a...

00:13:21.834 --> 00:13:25.000
-Dead bird cemetery.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:26.667
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:26.667 --> 00:13:30.000
♪♪

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.534
God's Love We Deliver
